    <string name="pc_keys_title">PC key chords</string>
    <string name="pc_keys_hint">Tap a chip to press that chord on the PC; long-press a chip to delete it. Use ctrl/alt/shift/win plus one key (a-z, 0-9, f1-f24, arrows, media keys). The Fn key lives in firmware and cannot be simulated. For fan/performance modes with G-Helper: bind its mode switch to a chord (e.g. ctrl+shift+f10) in G-Helper\'s keyboard shortcut settings, then save the same chord here.</string>
